{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false},"description":"Previews or applies one atomic configuration bundle of record types, fields, relationships, options and calculations. Preview does not write; apply takes the same bundle with expectedRevision and idempotencyKey, and a stale revision is rejected. Pending results are tracked as a durable operation. List, field, relationship and option names must be unique, compared case- and accent-insensitively, and names held by items in Trash count too; restoring or permanently deleting the trashed item frees its name. New definitions can use $client references; a new type takes $reference.name for its name field and has no other fields until they are added (notes are a richText field added with putField). Formulas use a bounded typed node list: children are defined before parents and root is selected. Related expressions evaluate in the linked record's context. Arbitrary code is not accepted. Currency fields require format.currency (three-letter code); changing it does not convert stored amounts. Type creation defaults to administrator-only access; delegated schema managers can use approved presets. Permissions and protected bindings remain enforced by the backend. Destructive changes can permanently remove data. delete moves a list, field or relationship to Trash, where it stays restorable for 30 days. The contact details field (shown in the app as the type Phone, email & social) is the field type channels: putField with valueType channels (input behavior, not required, not multiple, no options; at most one per list) holds phone numbers, email addresses and social profiles and lets messages match records by them. There are no phone or email field types; phone numbers and email addresses are stored in it as identities with provider phone or mail. Deleting it stops matching and keeps the identifiers until it is deleted permanently. A delete is sent without other operations in the bundle. The preview's deletion.cleaned and the apply result's deletionCleaned list the view, layout and widget references removed automatically; deletion.blockers lists calculations, parent access, bindings, routines and webhooks that must change first. Deleting a list moves widgets that measure it or show its activity to the same Trash batch. references names newly resolved IDs, not consumers. Deleting a field removes saved-view settings permanently; restoring it reports those settings but cannot recreate them. removed lists the data a permanent deletion erases. Items in Trash are not part of the model.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"action":{"enum":["preview","apply"],"type":"string"},"change":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"expectedRevision":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"idempotencyKey":{"maxLength":200,"minLength":8,"pattern":"^[^\\u0000]*$","type":"string"},"operations":{"items":{"oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"accessPresetId":{"anyOf":[{"anyOf":[{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"},{"pattern":"^\\$[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9_.-]{0,63}$","type":"string"}]},{"type":"null"}]},"description":{"maxLength":4000,"pattern":"^[^\\u0000]*$","type":"string"},"embedded":{"type":"boolean"},"icon":{"maxLength":64,"pattern":"^[^\\u0000]*$","type":"string"},"label":{"maxLength":200,"minLength":1,"pattern":"^[^\\u0000]*$","type":"string"},"navigationVisible":{"type":"boolean"},"operation":{"const":"createType","type":"string"},"pluralLabel":{"maxLength":200,"minLength":1,"pattern":"^[^\\u0000]*$","type":"string"},"reference":{"anyOf":[{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[8